===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A reduction in price.
#: {{ux|en|For the summer sale, there was 40% '''discount''' in all the stores at the mall.}}
#: {{ux|en|This store offers '''discounts''' on all its wares. That store specializes in '''discount''' wares, too.}}
# {{lb|en|finance}} A deduction made for interest, in advancing money upon, or purchasing, a bill or note not due; payment in advance of interest upon money.
# The rate of interest charged in discounting.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} A [[lack]] or [[shortcoming]].
#* {{RQ:Dickens David Copperfield|passage=On our approaching the house where the Misses Spenlow lived, I was at such a '''discount''' in respect of my personal looks and presence of mind, that Traddles proposed a gentle stimulant in the form of a glass of ale.}}
# {{lb|en|psychology|[[transactional analysis]]}} The act of one who believes, or act as though they believe, that their own feelings are more important than the reality of a situation.

